      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Change-impact assessment distinguishes justification of an assertion from validity of evidence under implementation, libraries, data, instruments, environments and governing assumptions. Delta includes material changes and discovery of invalid assumptions; I(Delta) conservatively covers changed facts and affected dependents; D*(t) covers transitive dependencies material to assertion, execution and reliance on check t. S_Delta = { t : D*(t) intersects I(Delta) } is a candidate reassessment selection. E_new combines retain_applicable(E_old, new_subject, new_basis) with actual E_reassessed.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":847,
          "quote":"S_Delta = { t : D*(t) intersects I(Delta) }.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#STDO%20Foundations%2FConstruction%20assurance%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20retention",
          "start_line":847
        },
        {
          "end_line":862,
          "quote":"E_new = retain_applicable(E_old, new_subject, new_basis) union E_reassessed.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#STDO%20Foundations%2FConstruction%20assurance%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20retention",
          "start_line":862
        }
      ],
      "key":"change_impact_evidence_retention",
      "label":"Change impact and evidence retention"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The workspace is continuing material construction state, including authoritative requirements, work products and durable records; material external state is observed through its owning interface. Actor context is a bounded, fallible, disposable acquired account. Acquisition, an authorised bounded operation, result observation and reacquisition form a resumable cycle.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":904,
          "quote":"The workspace is the continuing material state of the construction, including\nits authoritative requirements, work products and durable records. Material\nexternal state is observed through its owning interface. The actor's context is\na bounded account acquired from these sources. It is fallible and disposable.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#STDO%20Foundations%2FWorkspace%20and%20context",
          "start_line":901
        }
      ],
      "key":"workspace_context",
      "label":"Workspace, context and acquisition"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"The shared construction relation connects purpose, action, observation and correction. A denotes bound current material state; its acquired account includes workspace state, authoritative external observations, justified knowledge and explicit unknowns and may be incomplete or stale. Z denotes selected required outcome and acceptance conditions, potentially satisfied by many states; intermediate states are S0, S1, …, with a satisfying endpoint named separately. Specification, observation and predictive model respectively concern required conditions, actual conditions and possible intervention effects. Progress, preservation, termination and satisfaction are distinct claims; homeostasis names correction toward required conditions.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":978,
          "quote":"A is the current material state bound for construction. Its acquired account\ndescribes material workspace state, relevant authoritative external observations,\njustified knowledge and explicit unknowns; that account can be incomplete or\nstale. Z is the selected set of required outcome and acceptance conditions;\nmany states may satisfy it.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#STDO%20Foundations%2FBounded%20construction",
          "start_line":969
        }
      ],
      "key":"bounded_construction",
      "label":"Bounded construction"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"A configuration allocates operations and information to capable actors and declares material dependencies between their frames. Producing, checking and accepting are distinct responsibilities; functional decomposition, communication, authority and evaluation dependency are distinct relations. The optional Executive arrangement specializes the contract for longer-term delivery through bounded worker results and retains its own procedure and grants.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1071,
          "quote":"A configuration allocates operations and information to capable actors and\ndeclares the material dependencies between their frames.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#STDO%20Foundations%2FConfiguration",
          "start_line":1067
        }
      ],
      "key":"actor_configuration",
      "label":"Configuration"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["Arguments apply in the selected methodology domain and under their stated instance conditions."],
      "definition":"The derivation table groups decisions by consequence. Linked deciding bodies supply decisions; named consumers bind subjects and additional policy. Pillar contributions describe preserved relationships rather than derive every domain policy from F1–F6. The table claims neither world completeness nor a universal executor.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1096,
