        {
          "end_line":663,
          "quote":"1. declare the outcome traversal over typed assets\n2. publish the declarative GTL/ABG carrier structure\n3. implement only the minimal imperative adapter code that remains necessary",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.2A%20Outcome-First%20Realization%20Order",
          "start_line":661
        }
      ],
      "key":"outcome_first_realization",
      "statement":"ODD Products must use their edge-traversal compute unit to build operative framework behavior. Required order: declare outcome traversal over typed assets; publish declarative GTL/ABG carrier; implement only remaining necessary minimal imperative adapters. Before implementation declare source/target asset types, traversal/function name, closure/evaluation, lineage and ambiguity/gap obligations, and allowed F_D/F_P/F_H bindings. Carrier structure comprises GTL functions, typed nodes, vectors, operator/evaluator bindings, carrier schemas, policy/projection and lineage-ledger declarations. Imperative-first implementation later described with GTL vocabulary is ODD-shaped, not yet ODD-built.",
