      "conditions":[],
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":618,
          "quote":"They do not own runtime truth.\n\nThey also do not own continuation truth.\n\nDo not hide the real constructive carrier behind the word `service`.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F10.%20What%20An%20ODD%20Product%20Is%2FQuery%20And%20Service%20Layers",
          "start_line":614
        },
        {
          "end_line":753,
          "quote":"Discarding private actor context does not discard that workspace or require\nreplaying every historical body into the next actor's frame.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5%20Current%20State%20Is%20A%20Projection%20Over%20Constructive%20History",
          "start_line":752
        }
      ],
      "key":"projection_runtime_separation",
      "statement":"Service/query layers own neither runtime nor continuation truth and must not hide real constructive carriers behind service terminology. Visible current state is projection, never replacement/redefinition of ABG runtime facts. Fresh observations can expose divergence from earlier projections/beliefs and relevant evidence is admitted under existing authority. Discarding actor context does not discard workspace or require replaying all historical bodies into the next frame.",
      "uncertainty":""
