    {
      "applies_to_keys":["odd_product","abg_role"],
      "conditions":["At and across published traversal boundaries."],
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":786,
          "quote":"If an application attempts to replace ABG continuation with tenant-local\ncontrol flow, it is no longer behaving as an ODD application over GTL/ABG.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5A%20ABG%20Owns%20Continuation%20And%20Re-Entry",
          "start_line":783
        }
      ],
      "key":"abg_continuation_exclusivity",
      "statement":"ODD applications are cooperative subsystems, not replacement runtimes. ABG owns continuation authority, publication re-entry, graph-call lifecycle and graph step selection. Products must not own hidden continuation loops, carry multi-step controller memory across publish boundaries, infer later steps locally instead of ABG re-entry, treat public next and explicit graph-function continuation as rival authorities in one controller, or replace ABG with local orchestration. Tenant-local replacement of continuation is architectural drift from an ODD application over GTL/ABG, even if it publishes ODD-shaped artifacts.",
      "uncertainty":""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["odd_product","abg_role"],
      "conditions":["Any ODD Product over GTL/ABG changes runtime, start/iterate, worker transport, actor invocation, process supervision, plugin dispatch, event projection, closure, assurance, retry or continuation semantics."],
      "exceptions":["A different realization is lawful only in an explicitly ratified, non-overlapping runtime scope."],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":800,
          "quote":"The audit must prove that there is exactly one execution authority for the\naffected traversal. For a consumer using the GTL and ABG roles, that authority\nis the one consumer-bound realization of the ABG role.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5B%20Execution%20Authority%20Audit",
          "start_line":795
        }
      ],
      "key":"execution_authority_audit",
      "statement":"Before activation and closure, audit must prove exactly one execution authority for affected traversal: the consumer-bound ABG realization, even when that realization itself is under change. Inventory at least: traversal/vector selection (ABG owns; Product declares graphs/functions/assets/domain policy, never local next-step runner); invocation/supervision (ABG owns; Product provides bindings/prompts/payload/evidence adapters, never worker spawn/spawnSync/exec/timeout/kill/stdout-stderr supervision outside actor seam); retry/correction/continuation/re-entry (ABG owns; bounded outputs return control, never local loops/controller memory/hidden next); event emission/append/replay/projection (ABG owns; Product maps evidence into admitted payloads, never direct append/side ledger/bypassing reconstruction); closure/assurance gate (ABG with domain policy/gain inputs; Product provides interpretation/evaluators/gap reasons/weights, never worker self-report or postflight directly closing runtime unit). Artifact-only review is insufficient: include appropriate code, call-graph or static-surface review and name evidence ruling out hidden authority. Any local start/iterate traversal loop, outside-seam worker supervision, outside-ABG retry/continuation/re-entry state, unadmitted event/ledger mutation, plugin output carrying next-vector/closure/invocation/process/event authority instead of evidence/policy, or dual controllers is non-closure and means not currently ODD-correct, even if useful. Consequential entity-transformation admission specializes STDO-UP-016; broader execution/supervision/retry/projection retains existing ODD authority and is not reclassified as admission. F_P/F_H project generic candidate-producer/human-adjudication roles.",
      "uncertainty":"STDO-UP-016 and concrete runtime seams are referenced but not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["odd_projection_service"],
      "conditions":["Before publishing any ODD read model."],
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":858,
          "quote":"Publication\nfails closed on missing, stale or structurally divergent source truth. Compare\ninputs, outputs, vectors, declarations, ownership and closure law: name equality\ndoes not establish coherence. The projection's negative proof must exercise\nstructural drift as well as source absence. None of these publication bindings\ngrants runtime, closure or next-action authority.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5C%20Projection-Source%20Coherence",
          "start_line":853
        }
      ],
      "key":"projection_source_coherence",
      "statement":"Apply Faithful projection to concrete admitted source and consumer interpretation. Function catalogs preserve admitted GTL module/public carrier callable contract; ownership/start-target views preserve admitted carrier ownership/target relation derived from or structurally compared with it; runtime status preserves ABG facts/events/replay/projection truth; domain overlays preserve named admitted carrier under Product domain law. Publication fails closed on missing, stale or structurally divergent source truth. Compare inputs, outputs, vectors, declarations, ownership and closure law; equal names prove no coherence. Negative proof must exercise structural drift and source absence. Publication bindings grant no runtime, closure or next-action authority.",
      "uncertainty":"The full Faithful projection operation is external."
    }
